from _b4 import load, rep, insert_note, save, SRC
S = "making-plastic-releases-heat-unmaking"
t = load(S)
t = rep(t, "According to compliance advisers&rsquo; summaries, a notification of 19 January 2026 withdrew a temporary concession, granted by a Central Pollution Control Board notice of 28 November 2025, that had let producers use end-of-life certificates against their recycling targets. That leaves pyrolysis to fuel outside the recycling credit, but has no category for pyrolysis that returns monomer or feedstock to a cracker.</p>",
    "According to compliance advisers&rsquo; summaries, a notice of 19 January 2026 withdrew a temporary concession, granted by a Central Pollution Control Board notice of 28 November 2025, that had let producers use end-of-life certificates against their recycling targets; it was not an amendment to the Rules, whose amendment history in the Gazette runs from G.S.R. 73(E) of 23 January 2025 straight to G.S.R. 237(E) of 31 March 2026. "
    "That March amendment, the Plastic Waste Management (Amendment) Rules, 2026, redefines &ldquo;end of life disposal&rdquo; to include waste-to-oil conversion, but adds that it &ldquo;shall not include processes wherein plastic waste is converted into feedstock chemicals, or for the production of new plastic, which shall be considered as recycling&rdquo;. "
    "So pyrolysis to fuel stays outside the recycling credit, while pyrolysis that returns feedstock chemicals now counts as recycling. What the Rules do not say is how the Central Pollution Control Board will tell pyrolysis oil sold as fuel from pyrolysis oil sent to a cracker.</p>")
t = rep(t, "and should give pyrolysis oil that goes to a refinery or cracker as feedstock its own EPR category, distinct from pyrolysis to fuel, so that both routes are rewarded for what they return.</li>",
    "and the Central Pollution Control Board should set out how pyrolysis oil that goes to a refinery or cracker as feedstock is verified and credited as recycling under the March 2026 definition, distinct from pyrolysis to fuel, so that both routes are rewarded for what they return.</li>")
t = rep(t, "the January 2026 EPR notification is from compliance advisers&rsquo; summaries, not the gazette text, which this blog could not access.",
    "the January 2026 CPCB notice is from compliance advisers&rsquo; summaries; the Plastic Waste Management (Amendment) Rules, 2026 (G.S.R. 237(E), 31 March 2026, Gazette of India Extraordinary CG-DL-E-31032026-271465, egazette.gov.in/WriteReadData/2026/271465.pdf) were read in the Gazette&rsquo;s own text through " + SRC + ".")
t = insert_note(t, "The plastic section has been checked against the Gazette of India. The Plastic Waste Management (Amendment) Rules, 2026 (G.S.R. 237(E), 31 March 2026, CG-DL-E-31032026-271465) now count conversion of plastic waste into feedstock chemicals or new plastic as recycling, not end-of-life disposal. This piece had said the rules had no category for pyrolysis that returns feedstock; that was wrong, and the paragraph and the related proposal have been corrected. The 19 January 2026 instrument is a Central Pollution Control Board notice, not an amendment to the Rules.")
save(S, t)
